## 0. Prime Invariant
> Structure constrains interaction.
> Interaction produces dynamics.
> Dynamics produce capability.
> Therefore capability can often be redesigned by redesigning structure.
Matter is an enormous library of solved structural problems.
Physics and chemistry contain architectures for:
- transport
- storage
- resilience
- selectivity
- amplification
- isolation
- synchronization
- transformation
- self-assembly
- dissipation
- redundancy
- brittleness
- plasticity
- adaptation
- catalysis
- switching
- sensing
- threshold behavior
- distributed coordination
The objective is not:
`material -> superficial organizational analogy`
It is:
`material phenomenon
    -> causal structure
    -> abstract operator
    -> organizational instantiation
    -> measurable behavior
    -> observed delta
    -> refinement`
